</span><span>      context: `
</span><span>        B=E1=BA=A1n =C4=91ang design trading system cho Binanc=
e. H=E1=BB=87 th=E1=BB=91ng c=E1=BA=A7n handle=20
</span><span>        millions of user sessions v=E1=BB=9Bi real-time market=
 data. Each session=20
</span><span>        ch=E1=BB=A9a trading preferences, order history, v=C3=
=A0 risk management data.
</span><span>      `,
</span><span>     =20
</span><span>      question: `
</span><span>        L=C3=A0m sao b=E1=BA=A1n implement session management =
=C4=91=E1=BB=83:
</span><span>        1. Automatic cleanup khi users disconnect
</span><span>        2. Fast lookup performance cho active sessions =20
</span><span>        3. Memory usage kh=C3=B4ng grow indefinitely
</span><span>        4. Support concurrent access patterns
</span><span>      `,
</span><span>     =20
</span><span>      expectedThinking: `
</span><span>        Candidate should think through:
</span><span>        - Object lifecycle management (sessions c=C3=B3 indepe=
ndent lifecycle)
</span><span>        - Memory management (millions of sessions =3D potentia=
l leak risk)
</span><span>        - Performance requirements (fast lookup needed)
</span><span>        - Cleanup automation (manual cleanup error-prone at sc=
ale)
</span><span>        - Data structure choice (WeakMap vs Map vs hybrid)
</span><span>      `,
</span><span>     =20
</span><span>      strongAnswer: `
</span><span>        WeakMap-based approach:
</span><span>       =20
</span><span>        \`\`\`javascript
</span><span>        class TradingSessionManager {
</span><span>          constructor() {
</span><span>            // WeakMap for automatic cleanup
</span><span>            this.sessionData =3D new WeakMap();
</span><span>            this.riskProfiles =3D new WeakMap();
</span><span>           =20
</span><span>            // Regular Map for active tracking (enumeration)
</span><span>            this.activeSessionIds =3D new Map(); // sessionId =
-&gt; sessionObj
</span><span>          }
</span><span>         =20
</span><span>          createSession(userSocket) {
</span><span>            const sessionData =3D {
</span><span>              userId: userSocket.userId,
</span><span>              tradingPairs: new Set(),
</span><span>              riskLimits: { maxPosition: 100000 },
</span><span>              preferences: { orderType: 'limit' }
</span><span>            };
</span><span>           =20
</span><span>            // Store in WeakMap v=E1=BB=9Bi socket l=C3=A0m ke=
y
</span><span>            this.sessionData.set(userSocket, sessionData);
</span><span>            this.activeSessionIds.set(userSocket.sessionId, us=
erSocket);
</span><span>          }
</span><span>         =20
</span><span>          // When socket disconnects:
</span><span>          // =E2=9C=85 WeakMap auto-cleans session data
</span><span>          // =E2=9C=85 Manual cleanup of active tracking
</span><span>          onDisconnect(userSocket) {
</span><span>            this.activeSessionIds.delete(userSocket.sessionId)=
;
</span><span>            // sessionData auto-cleaned by WeakMap!
</span><span>          }
</span><span>        }
</span><span>        \`\`\`
</span><span>       =20
</span><span>        Benefits:
</span><span>        - Automatic memory management
</span><span>        - O(1) session lookup
</span><span>        - No manual cleanup complexity
</span><span>        - Memory scales with active users only
</span><span>      `,
</span><span>     =20
</span><span>      followUpQuestions: [
</span><span>        "L=C3=A0m sao handle reconnection scenarios?",
</span><span>        "Performance monitoring strategy?",
</span><span>        "Failover considerations cho session data?",
</span><span>        "Security implications c=E1=BB=A7a WeakMap usage?"
</span><span>      ]
</span><span>    };
</span><span>  }
</span><span> =20
</span><span>  static scenario2_FigmaCollaboration() {
</span><span>    return {
</span><span>      context: `
</span><span>        Figma editor c=E1=BA=A7n track collaboration state cho=
 thousands of design objects.=20
</span><span>        Multiple users c=C3=B3 th=E1=BB=83 select, edit, comme=
nt on objects =C4=91=E1=BB=93ng th=E1=BB=9Di.=20
</span><span>        Objects =C4=91=C6=B0=E1=BB=A3c create/delete frequentl=
y.
</span><span>      `,
</span><span>     =20
</span><span>      question: `
</span><span>        Design collaboration tracking system v=E1=BB=9Bi requi=
rements:
</span><span>        1. Track which users are interacting v=E1=BB=9Bi each =
object
</span><span>        2. Store collaboration metadata (cursors, selections, =
comments)
</span><span>        3. Automatic cleanup khi objects deleted from canvas
</span><span>        4. Real-time updates cho all collaborators
</span><span>      `,
</span><span>     =20
</span><span>      expectedThinking: `
</span><span>        Key considerations:
</span><span>        - Object-centric data (metadata tied to design objects=
)
</span><span>        - Dynamic object lifecycle (frequent create/delete)
</span><span>        - Memory management (thousands of objects =C3=97 multi=
ple users)
</span><span>        - Real-time requirements (performance critical)
</span><span>        - Automatic cleanup (manual tracking too complex)
</span><span>      `,
</span><span>     =20
</span><span>      strongAnswer: `
</span><span>        Multi-WeakMap architecture:
</span><span>       =20
</span><span>        \`\`\`javascript
</span><span>        class CollaborationManager {
</span><span>          constructor() {
</span><span>            // Object-centric tracking
</span><span>            this.objectSelections =3D new WeakMap(); // object=
 -&gt; Set of userIds =20
</span><span>            this.objectCursors =3D new WeakMap(); // object -&=
gt; Map(userId -&gt; cursor)
</span><span>            this.objectComments =3D new WeakMap(); // object -=
&gt; Array of comments
</span><span>           =20
</span><span>            // User-centric for enumeration
</span><span>            this.userSessions =3D new Map(); // userId -&gt; u=
serSessionData
</span><span>          }
</span><span>         =20
</span><span>          selectObject(designObject, userId) {
</span><span>            // Get or create selection set
</span><span>            let selections =3D this.objectSelections.get(desig=
nObject);
</span><span>            if (!selections) {
</span><span>              selections =3D new Set();
</span><span>              this.objectSelections.set(designObject, selectio=
ns);
</span><span>            }
</span><span>           =20
</span><span>            selections.add(userId);
</span><span>            this.broadcastSelection(designObject, userId);
</span><span>          }
</span><span>         =20
</span><span>          setCursor(designObject, userId, position) {
</span><span>            let cursors =3D this.objectCursors.get(designObjec=
t);
</span><span>            if (!cursors) {
</span><span>              cursors =3D new Map();
</span><span>              this.objectCursors.set(designObject, cursors);
</span><span>            }
</span><span>           =20
</span><span>            cursors.set(userId, { position, timestamp: Date.no=
w() });
</span><span>            this.broadcastCursor(designObject, userId, positio=
n);
</span><span>          }
</span><span>         =20
</span><span>          deleteObject(designObject) {
</span><span>            // Just remove object from canvas
</span><span>            // =E2=9C=85 All collaboration data auto-cleaned:
</span><span>            // - Selections auto-removed
</span><span>            // - Cursors auto-cleaned =20
</span><span>            // - Comments auto-removed
</span><span>            // =E2=9C=85 No manual tracking needed!
</span><span>          }
</span><span>        }
</span><span>        \`\`\`
</span><span>       =20
</span><span>        Benefits:
</span><span>        - Automatic cleanup khi objects deleted
</span><span>        - Fast collaboration lookups
</span><span>        - Memory scales with active objects only
</span><span>        - Simplified state management
</span><span>      `,
</span><span>     =20
</span><span>      followUpQuestions: [
</span><span>        "Conflict resolution cho concurrent edits?",
</span><span>        "Undo/redo implications?",=20
</span><span>        "Offline collaboration scenarios?",
</span><span>        "Performance v=E1=BB=9Bi large design files?"
</span><span>      ]
</span><span>    };
